docs/architecture/ui-v2/provenance.md:29:| P16 | Harness lifecycle 2 (mcp) reads an AES endpoint inventory (`CONVOS.mcp.tool` = `aes-inventory/get_endpoints`) and its follow-up is an AES policy review | The fixture reads the workspace MCP server inventory the core already exposes (`GatewayRead::McpServers`, C22) and the follow-up opens a Gateway guardrail review (`ChangeKind::GatewayGuardrails`) | AES has no admitted service (P18); the lifecycle stays read-only as in the prototype |
docs/architecture/ui-v2/provenance.md:31:| P18 | Six products are verified, inventoried and administered (AIS tool policies, AES discovered AI and policies, AES policy review `REVIEWS.aes`) | Only products with an admitted service are verified, inventoried or changed: Runtime Security (`ManagementResource`, `ChangeKind`), Gateway (`GatewayRead`, Gateway `ChangeKind`s), Red Team and Model/skill reads (C13, read-only). Agentic Identity Security and Agentic Endpoint Security render as "Not available in this release" with their dependency gate; no inventory, verification result or mutation is invented for them | The existing interfaces do not supply those product APIs; fixtures cannot establish a capability (parity matrix, C13 rule) |
docs/architecture/ui-v2/provenance.md:52:| P39 | `AdminInventory` generated from screens/administration-inventory.md | Implemented as a Rust table (`admin_inventory::inventory`) carried on `ShellSnapshot.administration` in the v2 shell only (null in the legacy shell, whose literal snapshot and leak canary are unchanged; the presentation's fixture copy is pinned to the table by a core test); a unit test and the `ui_v2_reviews` suite pin every offered (kind, action) to `changes::is_allowed` and every denied pair to its refusal, so a label can never outrun the core. Read and Change tabs render the retained views (the same reads and reviewed changes) embedded under the accordion with the inventory's labels; Unavailable tabs and products show their gate and nothing else; Removed tabs are not rendered. The Gateway MCP servers tab lists the chosen workspace's catalog through `listMcpServers` | One source of truth for dispositions, checked against the matrices the core enforces (V2-T20, V2-R11) |
docs/architecture/ui-v2/provenance.md:60:| P47 | The mcp lifecycle reads `GatewayRead::McpServers` directly (P16) | Its read-only call is a workspace MCP tool listing the workspace's MCP servers (`workspace_inventory.list_mcp_servers`), decided in the page like the other lifecycles; the desktop's own `GatewayRead::McpServers` listing stays in the MCP panel the Harness embeds | No desktop tool reads the Gateway MCP catalog; adding one would widen the Harness's tool surface beyond C22 |
